  "summary": "Recent items span haplotype-guided breeding, pangenome-aware GWAS, and deep learning for structural variation and cis-regulatory analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the move from linear reference-based analysis toward pangenome-aware and deep learning representations for plant genomic prediction and regulatory interpretation. PlantOmicsGWAS offers an open-source, reproducible Python framework for GWAS and genomic prediction supporting linear and pangenome references. A rice study finds a gene-based crop model closest to field observations, compared with GBLUP and CNN genomic prediction. Reviews address deep learning over pangenome graph and k-mer representations for structural variation-linked heritability in wild relatives, and over plant cis-regulatory sequence. HAPBDB instead applies haplotype-guided parental selection and cross design to QTL pyramiding in lettuce. The new element is representation beyond single linear references, though the items differ in whether they report primary results or reviews.",
